# Calibrate the board's gyroscope.
#
# An action rather than a service because it is slow and conditional: the
# gimbal must be physically still before calibration starts, and waiting for it
# to settle can take many seconds or never happen at all. A client needs to see
# which of those is going on and be able to give up.
#
# WARNING: calibrating a moving gimbal writes a wrong zero-rate bias into the
# board, and the result is a camera that drifts continuously afterwards. That
# is why the settle check exists and why this is never run automatically.
#
# Terminal states. A goal that is refused outright — motion not permitted, or a
# calibration already running — is rejected in the goal callback and never
# produces a Result at all, so there is no "rejected" result code here.
# Accepted goals end as:
#
#   SUCCEEDED  result_code == RESULT_OK
#   ABORTED    result_code == RESULT_NOT_STILL or RESULT_LINK_UNAVAILABLE
#   CANCELED   result_code == RESULT_CANCELLED
#
# Cancellation. Accepted freely during PHASE_WAITING_TO_SETTLE, because nothing
# has been sent to the board yet. Once PHASE_CALIBRATING begins the server does
# NOT report CANCELED until the calibration window has elapsed: a CMD_CONTROL
# would cancel the calibration on the board, but there is no frame this project
# has verified that confirms it aborted, and reporting CANCELED while the board
# may still be calibrating would be a false statement about hardware.

# Wait up to this long for the gimbal to go still. Zero means use the driver's
# configured default. Exceeding it aborts without calibrating — a gimbal that
# never settles must not be calibrated anyway.
builtin_interfaces/Duration settle_timeout

# Calibrate as soon as the request arrives, without waiting for stillness.
# Only for a caller that already knows the gimbal is stationary; the settle
# check exists for a reason.
bool skip_settle_check
---
# There is deliberately no separate `success` field. It could only ever
# duplicate result_code == RESULT_OK, and two fields that can disagree about
# the same fact are worse than one.
uint8 RESULT_OK=0
uint8 RESULT_NOT_STILL=1        # settle timeout expired while still moving
uint8 RESULT_LINK_UNAVAILABLE=2
uint8 RESULT_CANCELLED=3

uint8 result_code
string message

# How long the whole operation took, settle time included.
builtin_interfaces/Duration elapsed
---
# WAITING_TO_SETTLE -> CALIBRATING is the normal progression. With
# skip_settle_check set, the goal starts in CALIBRATING.
uint8 PHASE_WAITING_TO_SETTLE=0
uint8 PHASE_CALIBRATING=1

uint8 phase

# Largest angular movement seen between two consecutive telemetry samples, in
# radians. Meaningful while settling: it is the quantity being waited on, so a
# client can show why it is still waiting rather than just that it is. Held at
# the last observed value once calibration begins.
float32 motion

builtin_interfaces/Duration elapsed
